A||||6||DecadenceR||Whistling sound?||||1||
Z||000000||DecadenceR||07-23-2001||05:04 PM||||Okay. I don't get this. I re-did the gasked on my pushrod cover today because it was leaking. I put everything back together (I took of the intake because it was just easier than trying to get at it from under) and I took it for a small ride around the block to build up a temp and some pressure. Now the weird thing si, when the car was doing about 2000 rpm in first gear, nothing. But when it was in second gear at 2000 rpms, it sounded like there was almost a whistling type sound coming from the motor. I pulled over, looked, and there's nothing in the way of any belts. I shrugged, got back in, and started up again. And once again, in forst gear (automatic btw, 84 4cyl) at 2000 there was no sound, but in second gear I heard it again.<BR>Now the sound is almost like a whistle. But it's nt quite as pronounced. LIke if you were trying to whistle very quietly. I dunno. It's just weird. I never heard this before today. Any clue as to what it is?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||07-23-2001||05:18 PM||||Sounds like a vacuum leak to me.||||reg||6
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-23-2001||08:24 PM||||There's only one thing that i can think of. I checked all the vaccum lines and they're intact as far as I can tell. However, there are 2 that come off the passenger side of the TB... One of which goes to the EGR and the other goes to the vaccum line that runs along the backside of the trunk.<BR>So basically, can anyone confirm for me which one the line from the EGR goes to, the foward or the rear fitting? Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||07-23-2001||11:35 PM||||*BUMP*||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||07-24-2001||08:03 PM||||EGR forward.||||reg||1
Z||000005||k2m4||07-25-2001||11:56 AM||||hey deca this may be off the wall but it happened to me. you know the plastic mini fan that resides on your alternater behind the pully check that. I had some crap fall in my engine compartment and cracked them on my 2m4 and the thing sounded much like that a whistling whining sound. I checked everything and replaced everything with spare parts i had from the EGr to the vacuume line and it turned out it was that freakin alternater fan. When i reved ot up it whined like hell. replaced the alternater and i was good to go....just a shot in the dark but check it!<P>k<P>------------------<BR>Kerm<BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||DecadenceR||07-25-2001||02:21 PM||||Thanks a lot for the help guys, I'll double check both of those!||||reg||1
